Description:

Formula described by Buddhi at the Forums;

http://www.fractalforums.com/the-3d-mandelbulb/new-mandelbulb-like-formulas/

Use this code, for a triple rotation mandelbrot;

// Optimized by Luca GN, 25/11/2016; removed many unnecessary multiplications
double tempR = 0.; double temp = 0.;

//rotation around Z axis
tempR = 1.0 /sqrt(z.x * z.x + z.y * z.y);
temp = z.x * z.x - z.y * z.y;
z.y = 2.0 * z.x * z.y;
z.x = temp;
z.xy *= tempR; // only x and y must be changed
// and we don't do a double multip (unnecessary)

//rotation around X axis
tempR = 1.0 / sqrt(z.y * z.y + z.z * z.z);
temp = z.y * z.y - z.z * z.z;
z.z = 2.0 * z.y * z.z;
z.y = temp;
z.zy *= tempR;

//rotation around Y axis
tempR = 1.0 / sqrt(z.x * z.x + z.z * z.z);
temp = z.x * z.x - z.z * z.z;
z.z = 2.0 * z.x * z.z;
z.x = temp;
z.xz *= tempR;

z = z * length(z);
z += C; // the C constant vector, or the J-Seed.